<h1>Loophop Privacy Policy</h1>
<p class="mut">Last updated: October 19, 2026</p>
<p>This policy explains what information the mobile game Loophop (“the game”, “we”, “us”) collects, how it is used, and the choices you have.</p>
<p><strong>Developer:</strong> Jaakko Heikkinen<br><strong>Contact:</strong> <a href="mailto:heikkinen.j.jaakko@gmail.com">heikkinen.j.jaakko@gmail.com</a></p>

<h2>1. Information we collect</h2>
<p><strong>Information stored on your device.</strong> The game saves your progress on your device so it can remember it between sessions. This includes your best scores, gems, unlocked levels, skins, themes and music kits, missions and achievements progress, daily reward streak, and settings such as sound, music and vibration. This data stays on your device and is not sent to us. If you uninstall the game or clear its data, it is deleted.</p>
<p><strong>Accounts.</strong> The game does not require an account, and we do not ask for your name, email address, phone number, contacts, photos or precise location.</p>
<p><strong>Advertising data.</strong> The game shows ads. Our advertising partner, Google AdMob, may collect and use certain information to show and measure ads, such as your device’s advertising ID, IP address, device type and operating system, and information about how you interact with ads. Its handling of this data is described in its own privacy policy: <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">https://policies.google.com/privacy</a>.</p>

<h2>2. How we use information</h2>
<ul>
<li>To run the game and save your progress on your device.</li>
<li>To show ads, including rewarded ads you choose to watch, and to measure how ads perform.</li>
<li>To meet legal obligations.</li>
</ul>
<p>We do not sell your personal information.</p>

<h2>3. Sharing</h2>
<p>We share information only with the service providers described above, such as our advertising partner, and where the law requires it. The game’s share button uses your device’s share feature to send a short message about your score. What you share, and who you send it to, is your choice.</p>

<h2>4. Your choices</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Ad personalization:</strong> You can limit ad personalization or reset your advertising ID in your device settings (Android: Settings, Google, Ads; iOS: Settings, Privacy, Tracking).</li>
<li><strong>Delete your data:</strong> Use the “Reset progress” button in the game’s Settings, or uninstall the game.</li>
<li><strong>Rewarded ads are optional.</strong> You never have to watch an ad to play.</li>
</ul>

<h2>5. Children</h2>
<p>The game is intended for a general audience and is not directed at children under 13 (or the minimum age in your country). We do not knowingly collect personal information from children. If you believe a child has provided personal information, contact us and we will delete it.</p>

<h2>6. Your rights</h2>
<p>Depending on where you live, such as the European Economic Area, the United Kingdom or California, you may have rights to access, correct, delete or restrict the use of your personal data, or to object to its use. Since the game keeps its data on your device and we do not hold an account for you, most of these can be done directly in the game. For anything else, contact us at the address above.</p>

<h2>7. Data security and retention</h2>
<p>Progress data lives on your device and is protected by your device’s own security. Data held by our advertising partner is kept according to its policies.</p>

<h2>8. Changes to this policy</h2>
<p>We may update this policy from time to time. The “Last updated” date at the top will change when we do. Continued use of the game after an update means you accept the updated policy.</p>

<h2>9. Contact</h2>
<p>Questions about this policy: <a href="mailto:heikkinen.j.jaakko@gmail.com">heikkinen.j.jaakko@gmail.com</a></p>
